 "assumptions": [
  "M1-z is applied as the protocol writes it, on the 20 m grid of each area: z_vh = (VH after dB - dry mean dB) / dry spread dB.",
  "Permanent water is ESA WorldCover 2021 class 80; it is never flagged and is left out of the compared cells of every measure.",
  "The terrain answer comes first: HAND above the limit or a slope of 5 degrees or more is answered not flooded even where the radar has no value.",
  "A cell without a HAND or slope value that terrain does not answer gets no answer; the protocol does not name this case, it is a data gap.",
  "The no-answer share and the binding IoU are counted on the compared cells only; a cell without an answer counts as not flagged in the binding IoU.",
  "Test 1 of record (amendment 2): JAXA's layer whose name ends with _FLDEXT.geojson is the water and the layer ending with _REGION.geojson the observation area; both are put on the 20 m grid by cell centre.",
  "Compared cells: frame land (cell centre inside the 35 units, outside WorldCover class 80) whose centre lies inside REGION.",
  "The pass is the Sentinel-1C pass of 2025-07-28 about 11:20 UTC, because JAXA's files give no time with a zone (amendment 2); its VV and VH are raised by 0.79 dB before M1-z and the comparators run (amendment 1).",
  "The JAXA zips are read in memory and never extracted; their SHA-256 is checked against the protocol before the reading and after the scoring.",
  "The dry control of the binding rule is that of the first run (outputs/nan_case/test_result_v1.json); it does not depend on the test 1 reference.",
  "The 95% intervals come from 1000 draws of 2 km tiles (100 by 100 cells from the frame's north-west corner) with the seed recorded."
 ],
